I'm glad you brought this up because these folders are what separate a **student project** from a **commercial SaaS ERP**. Most of them are intentionally outside the Django app because they become independent services as your system grows.

Let me explain what each should eventually contain.

---

# 1. 📱 mobile/

This is **not** part of the React web frontend.

It is your Android/iOS application (React Native + Expo).

For construction companies, many employees rarely use a laptop.

For example:

- Site Engineers
- Storekeepers
- Foremen
- Safety Officers
- Drivers
- Plant Operators

should be able to use only the mobile app.

Example

```
mobile/
│
├── app/
│     Login
│     Dashboard
│     Attendance
│     Stock Requests
│     Daily Reports
│     Equipment
│
├── features/
│     attendance/
│     inventory/
│     planning/
│     quality/
│
├── services/
│     api.ts
│     auth.ts
│
├── offline/
│     sync.ts
│     queue.ts
│
└── assets/
```

Imagine a Site Engineer walking around the construction site.

He opens the mobile app.

He can

- take photos
- approve work
- request materials
- update activity progress
- sign inspections

without ever touching a laptop.

---

# 2. 📂 storage/

Right now Django stores uploaded files.

Later this folder becomes the logical organization of documents.

Example

```
storage/

company_documents/

    Licenses
    KRA
    NCA
    Contracts

project_documents/

    BOQs
    Contracts
    Specifications

drawings/

    Architectural
    Structural
    MEP

reports/

    Daily Reports
    Weekly Reports
    Monthly Reports

images/

    Site Photos
    Inspection Photos
    Progress Photos
```

Later this could move to

- AWS S3
- Azure Blob
- Cloudinary
- Google Cloud Storage

without changing your application logic much.

---

# 3. 📚 docs/

This isn't for users.

It's for developers and your business.

Example

```
